  "note": "Transcribed by hand from images, same method and same caveats as the FWD file beside it. Four things a reader has to know.\n\nTHE WINDOW IS INFERRED, NOT STATED. The sheet's column is headed \"FPL_Marcello's Next 5 Game Predicted Points\" under a 2026/27 banner and names no gameweeks. Two rows here overlap the FWD file, whose window IS stated as GW1-5, and both agree to rounding: Joao Pedro 21.1 here against 21.12 there, Calvert-Lewin 17.9 against 17.86. That is evidence the two artefacts describe the same window and the same projection, not proof. Pin it before grading with --score.\n\nNO PUBLICATION DATE. The screenshots do not show one and none has been invented. `posted` is null until somebody supplies it.\n\nCLUB NAMES ARE NORMALISED. The sheet spells clubs formally (\"Manchester City\"); matchPlayer resolves a club label against FPL's teams[].name, where the same club is \"Man City\". Left as published, every row would come back unmatched. The published label is kept in `teamAsPublished` so the transcription can be audited.\n\nONLY THE PROJECTION IS TRANSCRIBED. The sheet also carries 2025/26 points, minutes, points-per-game and his own Value metric. None of them is graded by anything here, and all but Value are re-derivable from the FPL API, so typing them in by hand would add 300 chances to be wrong in exchange for nothing.\n\nPARTIAL. These are the first 81 rows of a longer sheet. Absence from this file means not captured, never a projection of zero.",
